Attributes
	Attributes are the data members (variables) of a class that define the state or characteristics of an object. Every object has its own copy of the instance attributes.

Example
	Consider a Student class.
	class Student {
	    String name;
	    int age;
	    double marks;
	}
	Here name, age, marks are attributes.
	
Imagine a Car.

Its attributes are: Brand, Color, Model, Speed, Fuel Level.

Attributes describe what the object has.It stores data, represents it's state.

Instance Attributes vs Static Attributes
	Instance Attribute
		Each object gets its own copy.
	Static Attribute
		Shared by all objects.
		
Attributes are the variables declared inside a class that represent the state or characteristics of an object. They store the data associated with an object, and each object has its own copy of instance attributes. For example, in a Student class, name, age, and marks are attributes.

